From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 18:11:44 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Input: gemini-lid: apply the lid only after a system resume

Opening the lid wakes the system, and the switch's report reaches the
policy while devices are still resuming. Its work ran on the system
workqueue, which is not frozen, so it uninhibited the keyboard before
the keypad's own resume. The open started the keypad's scan; the
keypad's resume then found the device enabled and started it again,
and the second scan enabled the row interrupts a second time: one
"Unbalanced enable" warning per row on every lid-open wake. The first
scan also read the I2C expander before the expander had resumed.

Queue the work on system_freezable_wq. A lid change seen during a
suspend or resume then applies once tasks are thawed, after every
device has resumed. A close before a suspend still applies at once.
---
 drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
index 183ac9519..873eae73d 100644
--- a/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/gemini-lid.c
@@ -70,6 +70,11 @@ static void gemini_lid_work_fn(struct work_struct *work)
 		gemini_lid_apply(READ_ONCE(lid_closed));
 }
 
+/*
+ * Freezable, so that a lid opened during a system resume applies only once
+ * the resume is complete: uninhibiting the keyboard before its own resume
+ * starts it twice.
+ */
 static DECLARE_WORK(gemini_lid_work, gemini_lid_work_fn);
 
 static bool gemini_lid_is_keyboard(struct input_dev *dev)
@@ -89,7 +94,7 @@ static bool gemini_lid_filter(struct input_handle *handle, unsigned int type,
 		lid_armed = true;
 	if (lid_armed && lid_closed != !!value) {
 		WRITE_ONCE(lid_closed, !!value);
-		schedule_work(&gemini_lid_work);
+		queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &gemini_lid_work);
 	}
 
 	return false;
@@ -124,7 +129,7 @@ static int gemini_lid_connect(struct input_handler *handler,
 		scoped_guard(mutex, &lid_lock)
 			lid_keyboard = dev;
 		if (READ_ONCE(lid_closed))
-			schedule_work(&gemini_lid_work);
+			queue_work(system_freezable_wq, &gemini_lid_work);
 		return 0;
 	}
 
